{
  "id": 438537420,
  "iid": 22640,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Thrift: Enforce varint maximum length",
  "description": "thrift_get_varint_enc is not actually enforcing the maximum\nvarint length based into it; it is always using the int64\nlength, even when the int32 and int16 maximum lengths are passed\nin (so long as there is room left in the tvbuffer for a int64\nvarint.)\n\nThis resolves OSS-Fuzz 465909163 (although it is still possible\nfor field IDs to end up outside the valid int16 range if a value\nis close to the end of the range and then a delta takes it outside\nthe range; that is not checked. But as they are stored in a int64\nregardless, integer overflow is very very unlikely now.)",
